&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Technical Account Manager - Data.One&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This Technical Account Manager (TAM) role is part of the DataOne business within the ClearScore Group. The TAM demonstrates a balance of deep technical understanding and ability along with outstanding customer service and account management skills. This individual would have responsibility over the full partner lifecycle from onboarding, launch and ongoing maintenance.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The TAM role will work closely with the rest of the DataOne business which includes Product, Engineers, Analytics and Commercial counterparts in order to deliver the best experience to our partners.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The TAM’s main focusses will be setting up new Partners to start using DataOne open banking data, being on hand to assist partners with changes, and help drive the performance of their open banking usage.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you will be doing:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Relationship Management&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The main point of contact for our partner relationships after contracts are signed; working closely with our Commercial team to understand needs and goals of Partners.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Understand the Partners business objective and be able to be proactive in our approach to establish and maintain excellent partner relationships.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Attend and support our Commercial team in partner calls&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Assist in researching trends and insights around delivering best in class partner relationships.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Integration SME&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Onboard partners through the integration process, you will be the SME for each individual integration that they own and represent the voice of partners.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure that partners stay within the defined strategy of the DataOne team.

&lt;div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Weekly office requirement:&lt;/strong&gt; Monday/Wednesday weekly &lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Employment type:&lt;/strong&gt; Permanent&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Seniority level: &lt;/strong&gt;Mid-senior&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At GWI we’re always looking for extraordinary people who thrive on making an extraordinary impact. Right now we’re looking for a&lt;strong&gt; Product Manager &lt;/strong&gt;to play a key role in our &lt;strong&gt;User Management (Revenue&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&amp;amp; Enablement) &lt;/strong&gt;team in &lt;strong&gt;London&lt;/strong&gt;. If that’s you, and making a difference gets you out of bed in the morning, keep reading. It could be the start of something, well, extraordinary.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;br&gt;
&lt;h1&gt;Sounds great, what will I be doing? 🤔&lt;/h1&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As our Product Manager you&#39;ll own the systems that make GWI&#39;s subscription and consumption business run, such as billing, metering, user plans, feature access, product analytics and user messaging. It&#39;s the layer everything else sits on. Get it right and GWI can price, package and sell in new ways.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;br&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Two big pieces of work sit at the heart of this role. The first is billing for our consumption products, which is an area we&#39;re actively developing, and one you&#39;ll help shape. The second is making our internal tools talk to each other properly, so user data flows consistently between them and Salesforce, and everyone across the business is working from the same picture. Most of your stakeholders are internal - Revenue Operations, Finance, Business Intelligence, Client Success and Engineering - with some direct client contact along the way. You&#39;ll lead one squad of front-end and back-end engineers and a designer, alongside the PM and Engineers in our sister squad, Identity &amp;amp; Access - together you cover the whole of User Management.&lt;/p&gt;
